             <p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the JEE Main 2026 Session 1 response sheets and provisional answer keys today, February 4, 2026. This is a crucial moment for lakhs of engineering aspirants who appeared for the examination held from January 21 to January 29, 2026. Candidates can now access their recorded responses and compare them with the provisional answer key to calculate their probable scores and assess their performance. The answer key challenge window has also opened, providing a short window to raise objections if any discrepancies are found.</p>

             <div class="highlight-text">
                "Don't miss the opportunity to verify your performance and challenge any discrepancies in the provisional answer key. The challenge window is open only until February 5, 2026!"
             </div>

             <div class="section-title">Key Dates for JEE Main 2026 (Session 1 &amp; 2)</div>
             <p>Stay informed about all the important dates for both sessions of JEE Main 2026:</p>
             <div class="table-responsive">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                   <thead>
                      <tr>
                         <th>Event</th>
                         <th>Session 1 Dates</th>
                         <th>Session 2 Dates</th>
                      </tr>
                   </thead>
                   <tbody>
                      <tr>
                         <td>Exam Dates</td>
                         <td>January 21, 22, 23, 24, 28, 29, 2026</td>
                         <td>April 2 to 9, 2026 (Tentative)</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                         <td>Response Sheet &amp; Provisional Answer Key Release</td>
                         <td>February 4, 2026</td>
                         <td>Mid-April 2026 (Tentative)</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                         <td>Answer Key Challenge Window</td>
                         <td>February 4 to February 5, 2026</td>
                         <td>2-3 days after release (Tentative)</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                         <td>Final Result Declaration</td>
                         <td>By February 12, 2026</td>
                         <td>Late April 2026 (Tentative)</td>
                      </tr>
